    "body": "Shares proven Nx test results across pull requests through the pinned create-repo cache sidecar and merge promotion, while keeping package-version readers in small separate tiers. Release version/changelog edits preserve the other test hashes; dependency, source, feature and toolchain edits still invalidate them.\n\nEvidence being assembled on this draft: the promotion-branch and stacked release-edit demonstration have not run yet. The macOS release skip removal and its scheduling budget increase are provisional until that demonstration proves all four lanes replay. This draft is not ready for review or landing.\n\nLocal validation: the dedicated cache-contract Nx project passed all ten tests, including real Nx input mutations and base-input retention, unchanged next-release hashes, exact test partition, real pinned sidecar storage/read-only/promotion journeys, and the production cache-use command under onebudgetspec with simulated release selection. The version tier ran its four real tests. Workflow shape, publication path coverage, upstream digest parity, tier dependency checks, and scoped formatter checks passed. Final diff lint passed 52 rules with zero findings; scoped JavaScript lint and the final seven-test release-tail replay passed.\n\nThe cache-use threshold is a 100% design target, to revisit using the first published release after this change merges. No live release figure exists for an open draft. The eventual demonstration will use real executions and receipts behind explicitly simulated release selection.\n\nRecorded v0.64.0 release-cycle replay through onevcs measured 270679 seconds against 5400 seconds (onebudgetspec: over), measured at 2026-11-04T03:23:21Z because the saved publish job was in progress. Counted #563 and #564; omitted CI-only #566. This is a replay observation at that clock, not a historical completed-release duration.\n\nExpected release reruns include uncached tasks, release rehearsal/test, npm-launcher tests, the split version targets, and judged diff lint (its diff/base and llmlint fingerprint genuinely change). Cached task outputs are terminal output plus declared coverage/report files; release rehearsal writes no remote entry. No cache-size cap or source-scope deletion is introduced. All token REST access added for promotion is read-only (`actions: read`); runtime cache writes use the runner token.\n",
